===Etymology 1===
{{wp}}
{{ety|en|id=now|:inh|enm:present<ety:bor<fro:present>>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|present}}, from {{der|en|fro|present}}, from {{der|en|la|praesens|praesent-, praesens}}, present participle of {{m|la|praesum|praeesse|to be present}}, from {{der|en|la|prae-||pre-}} + {{m|la|sum|esse|to be}}. {{displaced|ang|andweard||present, current}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Relating to [[now]], [[for the time being]]; [[current]].
#: {{syn|en|current|Thesaurus:present}}
#: {{cot|en|future|past}}
#: {{ux|en|The [[barbaric]] [[practice]] continues to the '''present''' day.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''present''' [[manager]] has been here [[longer]] than the last one.}}
#: {{ux|en|up to the '''present''' day}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=12|passage=All this was [[extraordinarily]] [[distasteful]] to Churchill. It was [[ugly]], [[gross]]. [[never|Never]] [[before]] had he felt such [[repulsion]] when the [[vicar]] [[display]]ed his characteristic bluntness or coarseness of speech. In the '''present''' [[connexion]]&nbsp;{{...}} such [[talk]] had been [[distressingly]] out of place.}}
# Located in the [[immediate]] [[vicinity]].
#: {{syn|en|close|nearby|Thesaurus:near}}
#: {{ant|en|absent}}
#: {{ux|en|Only half of all present members were '''present''' at the meeting.}}
#: {{ux|en|Is there a doctor '''present'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|Several [[people]] were '''present''' when the event took place.}}
#: {{ux|en|Being the leader, Jason is always '''present''' at class.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Having an [[immediate]] effect (of a [[medicine]], [[poison]] etc.); [[fast-acting]]. {{defdate|16th|18th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|presentaneous}}
#: {{ant|en|slow-acting}}
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd|Alteratiues and Corials, corroborating, reſoluing the reliques, and mending the Temperament|2|5|1|subsection=5
|passage=Amongſt this [[number]] of [[cordials|Cordials]] and [[alterative|Alteratiues]], J doe not find a more '''preſent''' [[remedy]], then a cup of wine, or ſtrong drinke, and if it be ſoberly and opportunely vſed.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Not [[delayed]]; [[immediate]]; [[instant]].
#: {{syn|en|instantaneous|Thesaurus:instantaneous}}
#: {{ant|en|delayed|Thesaurus:delayed}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Measure|II|ii|passage=Sign me a '''present''' pardon for my brother,}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1636|author=w:Philip Massinger|title=w:The Bashful Lover|text=An ambassador{{...}}desires a '''present''' [[audience]].}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} Ready; [[quick]] in [[emergency]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''present''' wit}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[favorable|Favorably]] [[attentive]]; [[propitious]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Virgil|Pastoral 1
|passage=to find a [[god]] so '''present''' to my [[prayer]]}}
# {{senseid|en|deictic indicator}} Relating to something a person is referring to in the very [[context]], with a deictic use [[similar]] to the [[demonstrative]] adjective [[this]].
#: {{nearsyn|en|this#Determiner<pos:determiner>|this#Pronoun<pos:pron>|current#Adjective}}
#: {{ux|en|in the '''present''' [[study]]; the '''present''' [[article]]; the '''present''' [[results]]}}
# [[attentive|Attentive]]; [[alert]]; [[focused]].
#: {{syn|en|audient|heedful|reckful}}
#: {{ant|en|distracted|inattentive}}
#: {{ux|en|Sorry, I was [[distracted]] just now, I'll try to be more '''present''' from now on.}}
# {{lb|en|politics}} Neither [[for]] or [[against]] (used in voting to express [[abstention]]).

