====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To bring (someone) into the presence of (a person); to [[introduce]] [[formally]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''present''' an envoy to the king}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To appear or represent oneself outwardly.
#: {{usex|en|With your shabby attire, you do not '''present''' well as a prospective investment banking associate!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To nominate (a member of the clergy) for an ecclesiastical [[benefice]]; to offer to the bishop or ordinary as a candidate for institution. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To offer (a problem, complaint) to a court or other authority for consideration. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|now|rare}} To [[charge]] (a person) with a crime or accusation; to bring before court. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive}} To come forward, [[appear]] in a particular place or before a particular person, especially [[formally]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Job|1|6|passage=Now there was a day when the sons of God came to '''present''' themselves before the lord.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put (something) forward in order for it to be seen; to [[show]], [[exhibit]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Rape of the Lock|passage=So ladies in romance assist their knight, / '''Present''' the spear, and arm him for the fight.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make clear to one's mind or intelligence; to put forward for consideration. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal| en| date=2012-01| author=Steven Sloman| title=The Battle Between Intuition and Deliberation| volume=100| issue=1| page=74| magazine=w:American Scientist| url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/the-battle-between-intuition-and-deliberation| passage=Libertarian paternalism is the view that, because the way options are '''presented''' to citizens affects what they choose, society should '''present''' options in a way that “nudges” our intuitive selves to make choices that are more consistent with what our more deliberative selves would have chosen if they were in control.| accessdate=12 May 2013| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120108050233/http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/the-battle-between-intuition-and-deliberation| archivedate=8 January 2012}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[put on]], [[stage]] (a play etc.). {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|The theater is proud to '''present''' the Fearless Fliers.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|military}} To [[point]] (a firearm) at something, to hold (a weapon) in a position ready to fire. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive}} To [[offer]] oneself for mental consideration; to [[occur]] to the mind. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|Well, one idea does '''present''' itself.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|medicine}} To come to the [[attention]] of [[medical]] [[staff]], especially {{m|en|with}} a specific symptom. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|The patient '''presented''' with insomnia.}}
#: {{usex|en|Symptoms typically '''present''' in early childhood.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|medicine}} To appear (in a specific way) for [[delivery]] (of a fetus); to appear first at the mouth of the [[uterus]] during childbirth. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|with "as"}} To appear or represent oneself (as having a certain gender).
#: {{ux|en|At that time, [[w:Lili Elbe|Elbe]] was '''presenting''' as a man.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To act as [[presenter]] on (a radio, television programme etc.). {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Anne Robinson}} '''presents''' "{{w|The Weakest Link (UK game show)|The Weakest Link}}".}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[give]] a [[gift]] or [[presentation]] to (someone). {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|compliment|bestow}}
#: {{ux|en|She was '''present'''ed with an honorary degree for her services to entertainment.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[deliver]] (something abstract) as though as a [[gift]]; to [[offer]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''presented''' my compliments to Lady Featherstoneshaw.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To hand over (a [[bill]] etc.) to be [[paid]]. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|zoology}} To display one's [[female]] [[genitalia]] in a way that [[signal]]s to others that one is ready for [[copulation]]. Also referred to as {{w|lordosis behaviour}}. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
# {{lb|en|fandom slang}} In [[omegaverse]] [[fiction]], to have one's secondary [[sex]] ([[alpha]], [[omega]], or [[beta]]) become apparent, typically at [[puberty]]. {{defdate|from 21st c.}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}

